Baselaird was one of [[Eathon Lambert|Eathon Lambert's]] strongest Titans and was later recovered by his son, [[Lok Lambert]], at the [[Temple of Poseidon]] near the entrance to [[Atlantis]] after the team solved a riddle, left to him by his dad using a box only Lok could see. Lok later invoked it after sensing his name through the [[Titans|bond]]. {{Source|The Unseen Guide}} Later, in Atlantis, Baselaird was summoned by a raging Lok in his one-on-one fight against [[Rassimov]]. He helped defeat [[Thornment]] and fought against [[Sekhmet]]. He then tackled [[Anubian]] to the [[Casterwill family|Casterwill]] compound's entrance, which the [[Atlantis Guardian]] closed at Lok's orders, instantly sending Anubian back to its amulet. {{Source|Coming of Age}}

On the team's way to the [[Golden Asp]], Lok again summoned Baselaird after being grabbed by [[Unnamed Suit 040]]'s [[Bonelasher]]. He quickly sent the [[Suits|Suit]]'s Titan back to its amulet by stomping on it after a poor attempt from Bonelasher to slash Baselaird's shield. {{Source|The Golden Asp}}

In the ambush to recover the [[Legendary Titans]] from the team, this Titan was invoked by Lok to fight off [[Shauna]] and her Titans in the streets of Venice. However, he was swiftly paralyzed by her [[Dervish]]. {{Source|The Secret of Two Generations}}

Baselaird was used to launch [[Dendras]]' marionettes torwards [[Overlos]] in the final battle against [[the Professor]], making Lok be able to control Overlos after [[Archwarder]] disrupted the Professor's control of the Legendary Titan. {{source|The Mission}} 

Lok became [[Titans#Powerbonding|Powerbonded]] with Baselaird during a [[Fate of the Father|mission]] of great personal importance to him, summoning him to fight against [[the Organization]] outside the [[Nexus]] in [[Peru]]. Lok ordered him to use Sword Strike against a [[Gigadrone]] Titan and also defeat [[Hoffman]]'s [[Myrmidon]], making [[Wilder]] and his group retreat. {{source|Doorway to Huntik}}

Inside the secret chamber of the [[Tower of Nostradamus]], Lok summoned Powerbonded Baselaird to fight the Organization. In response, Wilder invoked [[Incubane]] and the two [[Titans]] fought until Hoffman hit Lok with [[Poisonfang]], making Powerbonded Baselaird briefly fall to his knees; ultimately, both Titans sent each other to their respective amulets. {{Source|The Tower of Nostradamus}}

[[Cherit]] managed to sneak Powerbonded Baselaird's amulet inside the Organization vehicle Lok and [[Sophie Casterwill]] were trapped in, and the Titan was invoked to break open the car from the inside. [[Unnamed Suit 055]] later fired a Raypulse against Baselaird's shield, who responded by sending him flying by striking him with his shield. {{Source|Chasing Void}} 

Lok again used Powerbonded Baselaird inside [[Klaus' bookshop]] to fight off the Organization in the search for [[Void]]'s amulet. He took out a Redcap Titan with his Shooting Slash ability after a long struggle, then swiftly sent a Gigadrone Titan back to its amulet as the team started heading to the underground laboratory. {{Source|The Blood Spiral}}

Powerbonded Baselaird was summoned by Lok to fight off the three Titans invoked by [[Arc]] next to the [[Cathedral of Notre Dame]] after he struggled to do so with the [[Willblade]]. He helped Lok defeat [[Ironsquire]] by shattering part of his shield and also took out [[Freelancer]]. Later on, Lok attempted to again invoke Baselaird inside Arc's dream to fight multiple [[Harlekin|Harlekins]] after his Freelancer turned into a Harlekin Titan; however, summoning Baselaird only made another one appear. {{Source|The Legendary Titan of Fate}}

ON [[Medusa's Island]], Powerbonded Baselaird was used to battle [[Kiel]] and the [[Casterwill Hunters]]. He fought multiple [[Harlekin|Harlekins]] and later Kiel's [[Vulcana]]. After a long struggle, Baselaird grabbed Vulcana's fiery body with his hand, taking her out but also being sent back to his amulet in the process. {{Source|Zhalia's Mission}}

This Titan was again invoked by Lok in the [[Phoenix Volcano]] in an ambush against [[Shauna]] and [[Wind]]. He grabbed Wind so that Lok could restrain him with [[Ropetrick]]. After the two [[Blood Spiral]] Seekers freed themselves, Powerbonded Baselaird fought the powerful [[Shakrit]], without much success; later, he defeated [[Ash]] by throwing her torwards a lava pool and briefly struggled against [[Lilith the Queen]]. In order to finally defeat Shakrit, Lok used Baselaird's Focus Blade ability so that Baselaird could lend him his Powerbonded energy. {{Source|The Phoenix's Ashes}}

Powerbonded Baselaird was again summoned to help [[Dante Vale]] and [[Grier]] against the two [[Undergolem]] Titans invoked by [[Eathon the dog]] in [[the Professor's castle]]. In the long battle that followed, he took out the two Undergolems as well as [[Hoffman]]'s [[Doberman]]. After Lok managed to retrieve [[Rassimov's files]] from the castle, he called Baselaird back to his Amulet. {{Source|An Ally from the Organization}}

As the team waited for information on the [[Spiral Mark]]'s location, Lok invoked Powerbonded Baselaird to fight [[Psikofen]] by [[Nostradamus' Tomb]]. After a tense standoff between the Titans, Baselaird waited for Psikofen to charge before defeating him. Lok then called him back to his amulet. {{Source|Words from Eathon}} At the Spiral Mark, Baselaird was again summoned to hold off [[Legion]] but was overpowered by the Legendary Titan. He was nearly permanently absorobed but Lok ordered him to return to his Amulet just in time. {{Source|The Spiral Mark}} Later, during the battle between the Foundation, Casterwills and the Blood Spiral, Lok invoked Baselaird to fight off two [[Marauder|Marauders]]; after defeating the two Titans, Lok called him back to his Amulet. {{Source|Lok and the Betrayer}}

[[File:S2E35 Lok Harlekin Baselaird Vulcana.png|thumb|'''Total Defense''' is used to protect [[Lok Lambert|Lok]] from [[Vulcana]]'s fire]]
When the bond with his Seeker became stronger, Baselaird became stronger as well as changing significantly in appearance. Where his armor was originally mostly brown and covered a majority of his body, golden armor now predominantly covers his torso with a long red cape attached to it, and a portion of his legs with golden boots while some skin can be seen on his arms and legs. His helmet - where it once showed his eyes along with five small spikes, changed to have three long, curved spikes protruding from it, now concealing his eyes. He became able to communicate with his Seeker via telepathy and respond to his commands. Baselaird's shield and sword both became considerably larger in size. In contrast, his sword became attatched to his arm, which can make him vunerable in case it gets stuck. {{Source|Lok and the Betrayer}} His Powerbonding abilities include:
*'''Double Aggression''' - enhances his combat skills when facing off two or more enemies. {{source|The Legendary Titan of Fate}} {{Source|Zhalia's Mission}} 
*'''Focus Blade''' - allows Baselaird to lend all of his energy to his Seeker so as to enhance their offensive strikes. {{Source|The Phoenix's Ashes}}
*'''Leading Charge''' - enables him to charge at an enemy at speed from a distance. {{Source|The Phoenix's Ashes}} {{Source|The Spiral Mark}}
*[[File:S2E45 Lok Focus Blade.png|thumb|[[Lok Lambert|Lok]] absorbs Baselaird's powerbonded energy using '''Focus Blade''']]'''Shooting Slash''' - fires a powerful ray of energy directly from his sword  {{Source|The Tower of Nostradamus}} {{Source|The Blood Spiral}} or by striking the ground with it. {{Source|The Legendary Titan of Fate}} Alternatively, it can swipes an enemy with his sword with additional power. {{Source|The Phoenix's Ashes}} {{Source|Lok and the Betrayer}}
*'''Sword Strike''' - Baselaird swipes an enemy with his sword. {{Source|Doorway to Huntik}}
*'''Total Defense''' - uses his shield to completely cover himself from incoming attacks. {{Source|The Tower of Nostradamus}} {{Source|Zhalia's Mission}}
{{clear}}

